Artwork
-------

Most of the artwork here was drawn for this project and is GPL-3.0-or-later
with the rest of it: the three-cover mark, the monitor and the television, the
reboot arrow, the Windows panes, and every tile background.

The rest is other people's, vendored into assets/marks/ and rendered into the
tiles under assets/tiles/. It is redistributed with this program under the
terms below.

    Steam roundel      from Sunshine's own steam.png (LizardByte)  GPL-3.0
    Heroic shield      Heroic Games Launcher, public/icon.png      GPL-3.0
    Tux                Larry Ewing, Simon Budig, Garrett LeSage    Attribution
    Arch "Crystal"     Arch Linux                                  GPL
    Debian swirl       Debian OpenLogo                             CC BY-SA 3.0
    Fedora icon        Fedora                                      public domain
    Linux Mint mark    Linux Mint                                  CC BY 3.0
    Ubuntu circle      Canonical                                   GPL-3.0

The Apple mark is not vendored as artwork but rendered from the path Apple
publishes in the global navigation on apple.com. It is used nominatively, to
say that a tile starts the desktop of a Mac, and for nothing else.

These are trademarks of their respective owners -- Valve Corporation, the
Heroic Games Launcher project, Linus Torvalds, Apple Inc., Microsoft
Corporation, and each distribution's project or company. They are used only to
identify the software or platform a tile launches. No affiliation with,
sponsorship by, or endorsement from any of them is claimed or implied. If you
own one of these marks and would rather it were not used here, open an issue
and it will be removed.

docs/tile-art.md records how each one is used, and carries a reminder to check
before each major release that a mark is still the current one.


Upstream
--------

The engine (src/sunshine_apps_ui/core) began as bazzite-sunshine-manager by
wadiebs, by way of 4o66's fork of it, and was folded into this project rather
than kept as a separate program alongside it. It is derived from

    https://github.com/wadiebs/bazzite-sunshine-manager

built on commit 4bedee5 (2026-04-19), which upstream calls version 2.0.

That work is licensed under the MIT License, and its notice is preserved
verbatim in LICENSE.upstream-MIT, exactly as upstream published it -- including
its copyright line, which names no holder. Nothing here relicenses it: upstream's
code remains available from upstream under MIT, and the MIT terms continue to
apply to it.

What is licensed under the GPL is this fork's own additions and the combined
work they form. The MIT License permits that: it allows a derivative to be
distributed under other terms provided its copyright and permission notice are
retained, which is what LICENSE.upstream-MIT is for.

One consequence, recorded so it is not rediscovered the hard way: patches from
this fork can no longer be offered to upstream, because an MIT project cannot
take GPL code without relicensing. Two pull requests were filed before this
change (wadiebs/bazzite-sunshine-manager#34 and #35); those were offered to an
MIT project and remain MIT. Anything sent upstream from here on would have to be
offered separately under MIT.
